<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="9c6c51dc">&lt;p&gt;
    INVEST should be used to build valuable and quality Backlog Items such as a User Stories or features. Consider the
    INVEST mnemonic so these items&amp;nbsp;are:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;I - Independent&lt;/strong&gt; of other Backlog Items&lt;br /&gt;
    Product Owners should be able to change the ordering of Backlog Items in response to a changing environment (e.g.,
    client needs, market conditions, etc.) and this is easier to achieve with little or no dependencies. This also allows
    for easier planning.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;N - Negotiable&lt;/strong&gt; such that they are a statement of intent and not an explicit contract&lt;br /&gt;
    Backlog Items will be worked on and further refined so they should be formatted in such a way that they can be adjusted
    to incorporate newly learned information. Meaning the basic need and intent should be captured as opposed to a detailed
    description of a solution.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;V - Valuable&lt;/strong&gt; to the stakeholders&lt;br /&gt;
    Every Backlog Item should bring value to the stakeholders, either directly or indirectly, via risk mitigation or
    enabling other dependent high-value Backlog Items.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;E - Estimable&lt;/strong&gt; so that the work can be sized&lt;br /&gt;
    Both the work to be done as well as the results to be achieved should be clear enough so that the size of the Backlog
    Item can be estimated.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;S - Small&lt;/strong&gt; enough to fit within a single sprint&lt;br /&gt;
    Any Backlog Item should be small enough to be completed within a single sprint before it can be worked on. Only the top
    portion of the Product Backlog needs to be small. The remainder can stay large until an item moves toward the top of
    the Product Backlog and is ready to be decomposed, as Backlog Items are successively delivered.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;T - Testable&lt;/strong&gt; in order to confirm quality&lt;br /&gt;
    It should be clear how to verify whether the results of the work fulfilled the original need as captured by the Backlog
    Item.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
